WEBVTT

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:04.290
It is the turn of the 20th century.

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:10.080
The Kingdom of Albion's new royal air force,
commonly known as the Air Fleet,

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.040
has created a dramatic shift
in the balance of global power.

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:17.000
With its monopoly on Cavorite,
and the Air Fleet at its command,

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.880
the Kingdom of Albion became
the greatest world power since the Roman Empire.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:24.500
However,

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:28.330
revolution split the kingdom into East and West,

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:33.330
with the London Wall separating the Kingdom of Albion
from the Commonwealth of Albion.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:41.830
Ten years later, London became the front line
of a secret war fought between the nations' spies.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:11.960
Wh-who are you?

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:15.830
Just a passing extraterrestrial.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:17.710
What?

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.330
I am from the Black Lizard Planet.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.920
If you're going to joke, do it somewhere else!

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:28.540
I'm not joking.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:29.670
I'm just lying.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:33.750
There he is!

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:53.210
Is that... Cavorite?

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:55.170
Impossible... at that size...

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:26.380
Um...

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:40.790
Incoming. One vehicle!

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:42.790
Okay, we're out of here.

00:04:58.420 --> 00:04:59.790
They were ready for us.

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:02.420
Who are you people?

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:06.250
We're under orders to keep you safe
until you find asylum in the West.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:09.080
Then... you're with the Commonwealth?

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:11.880
Hm? Didn't you tell him, Ange?

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:13.290
I did.

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:15.830
I told him we're from the Black Lizard Planet.

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:17.210
You mean we're spies!

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:38.210
Are you spies always doing this kind of thing?

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:40.540
Well, sometimes.

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:43.670
Refrigeration complete.

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:46.170
We'll use it when we get out of here.

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:47.130
Understood.

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:11.460
Welcome back.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:14.830
Thanks.

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:15.960
Now then...

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:18.170
We've shaken them off. Ready to go back?

00:06:18.170 --> 00:06:19.170
Back?

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:20.290
Back where?

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:23.420
To the perfect place to hide you.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:35.540
So I found an envelope in my bag.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:36.960
An envelope?

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:41.130
Yup. I was so afraid my cover was blown,
but then I saw the flower on it.

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:41.960
Flower?

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:44.580
New orders, right?

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:48.040
You workaholic! Try to enjoy being a student.

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:50.500
So? Who was it from?

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:52.750
Lord Rupert's second son.

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:55.880
It said to meet him behind the gymnasium after school.

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:57.290
A challenge to a duel?

00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:58.920
It was a love letter!

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:00.000
Um.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.460
Where are we?

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:02.540
At school.

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:05.500
A very formal and prestigious academy.

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:08.250
Members of the royal family go here.

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:10.250
Why did we come here?

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:11.460
"Why"?

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:18.790
Because we're students here.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.000
Welcome back, everyone.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.670
Oh, are you the defector?

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:32.380
Pleased to meet you. I am-

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:33.040
I know!

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:35.880
Everyone in the Kingdom knows...

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:40.250
You can't mean... you're a spy, too?

00:07:40.630 --> 00:07:42.000
Princess?

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:44.250
Yes, I am a spy.

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:51.880
Our Principal Team has secured asylum seeker E.

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:55.040
They are currently hiding him at
Queen's Mayfaire Academy.

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:56.330
What a waste.

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:59.250
The Princess should be used for more important things.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:02.460
What about the Wall Team?

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:04.710
This is the shift schedule.

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.540
Tell both teams.

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:13.290
They'll cross the Wall next Thursday.

00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:33.790
Good morning!

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:38.630
Is our school that fascinating?

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:43.380
Oh, sorry. I shouldn't let anyone see me, should I?

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:45.670
If you know that, then be careful.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:49.960
An omelet?

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:52.000
It's the only thing I can make.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:54.960
That's okay, I like them. Thank you.

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:57.710
Mm, delicious!

00:08:58.460 --> 00:09:00.920
We're coordinating a date for your crossing.

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:03.040
You'll be staying here until it's decided.

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:06.170
Why...

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:09.420
Why would a girl like you be a spy?

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:13.920
When I was born, the word "spy"
was written on my forehead.

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:17.000
Are all the lies because you're a spy, too?

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:19.710
The truth wouldn't be very interesting.

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:23.500
What's that?

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:25.000
A chamber pot.

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:25.880
What?!

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:26.500
That?

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:30.290
Oh.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.540
Another lie?

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:34.330
Tell me if there's anything else you need.

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:36.170
I'll get you anything I can.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:39.210
Even a person?

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:43.460
Can you get me a person?

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:46.210
He wants his little sister?

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:48.210
It's not like getting opera tickets.

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:51.210
You can't just say,
"I'd like to add one more to the party."

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:54.580
Do you think he will threaten not to defect without her?

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:55.960
He already did.

00:09:56.170 --> 00:09:57.960
That's that, then!

00:09:57.960 --> 00:09:59.830
Defectors to the West, party of two!

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:01.830
You make it sound so easy.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.420
What do we do, Ange?

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:08.670
What do you suppose they're talking about?

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:09.750
Their escorts for the soiree?

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:10.880
Oooh!

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:14.750
Drug Eric and carry him over the Wall alone.

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:15.920
Aww, but...

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:18.790
Good idea. We shouldn't take the risk.

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:22.670
Are you sure we couldn't let them
defect together anyway?

00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:26.460
I mean, it would be so sad to tear them apart.

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:32.130
Princess, I understand how you feel, but-

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:32.750
I'll gather intel.
Princess, I understand how you feel, but-

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:33.750
I'll gather intel.

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:37.710
I'll find the sister and figure out
whether she wants to defect.

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:38.920
And I'll get more info on Eric.

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:39.420
Come on, Ange...
And I'll get more info on Eric.

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:40.540
Come on, Ange...

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:42.790
We still have four days until Thursday.

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:44.040
Oh, good!

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:46.000
Thank you, Ange!

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:06.540
So Eric's little sister is in the hospital up ahead?

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:10.790
Yes. And we had to shake off some pursuers last night,
so there might be an ambush, too.

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:46.710
Brother?

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:49.670
Why didn't you come yesterday?

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:53.210
Hello. You must be Miss Amy.

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:54.330
Who are you?

00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:57.380
I came to deliver some flowers from Eric Anderson.

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:00.380
Flowers?

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:01.630
Oh, yes!

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:03.420
See? They're very pretty!

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:05.380
Is he a relative of yours?

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:07.670
What do you really want?

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:09.960
I know you're lying!

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:11.670
Those aren't from my brother!

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.750
Cavorite poisoning?

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:15.580
Who are you?!

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:18.670
How dare you use my brother's name to trick me!

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:22.420
My brother is all I have left!

00:12:22.710 --> 00:12:25.750
Get out of my sight! Get out!

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:33.790
Apparently Miss Amy was in a Cavorite accident.

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:37.670
And it's going to take rather a lot of money
to pay for an operation.

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:48.000
Why don't you go on back without me?

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:49.250
What are you going to do?

00:12:49.250 --> 00:12:51.580
Go back to the Black Lizard Planet?

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:53.920
I'm getting insurance. Just in case.

00:12:59.790 --> 00:13:01.130
An insurance office?

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:02.130
Yes, Miss.

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:05.920
I can never tell how much of what she says is true.

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:08.080
I don't think she knows, either.

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:08.920
What?

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:13.420
But some lies become truth in the telling.

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:20.630
I don't believe this.

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:23.250
Now I have to forge documents for two people.

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:24.170
There's no helping it.

00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:26.420
Dorothy! What are you writing?

00:13:26.580 --> 00:13:29.630
An essay of apology. Do you girls want to help?

00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:30.960
We'll pass.

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:32.960
See you at the match next week.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.040
That was a bold move.

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:38.000
It's best not to sneak around with these things.

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:42.500
I see Ange isn't the only one with a knack for lying.

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:44.750
Spies are all liars.

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:47.710
You're lying to me now, Chise.

00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:49.500
As are you.

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:55.290
So what do you say we try
being honest with each other?

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:57.790
The idea has its charm.

00:13:57.790 --> 00:14:01.250
But if we stopped lying,
we wouldn't be able to stay friends.

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:03.500
Is that really friendship?

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:05.670
Even parents and children lie to each other.

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:12.330
Ange?

00:14:13.630 --> 00:14:17.210
Your sister's operation. Is that why you're defecting?

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:20.330
So you saw her.

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:21.170
You met Amy.

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:24.290
She said she didn't want any flowers
and chased us out.

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:27.290
Since the accident, it's like she's a different person.

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:31.920
Until then, she was a nice girl, always smiling.

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:34.830
But now... You'll need money for the operation.

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:37.540
Ten years' salary.

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:39.330
There's no way I can afford it.

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:42.290
But then, a man I'd never met paid me a visit.

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:47.380
He said that if I defected to the Commonwealth
with my research, he would give me the money.

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:49.250
The timing is just too perfect, isn't it?

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:52.210
Tell me, Ange.

00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:54.630
Was my sister really in an accident?

00:14:55.330 --> 00:15:00.580
If I weren't a scientist, would my sister
have been spared this suffering?

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:04.960
Spies are told only what they need to know,

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:07.880
so I can't deny that possibility.

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:11.080
Spies aren't champions of justice, after all.

00:15:11.710 --> 00:15:13.670
So NOW you're being honest.

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:16.670
Even if it was a lie,

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:18.540
I wish you'd tell me it was an accident.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:22.250
So... would you like to go outside?

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:28.290
The stars are so beautiful here.

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:29.080
Yes.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:31.420
Do you hate me?

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:33.130
Why?

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:37.540
I betrayed my research team for money.

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:40.250
You care about your family.

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:41.290
I understand.

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:43.130
I had a family, too.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:44.630
"Had"?

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:47.710
I watched as my parents were murdered.

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:50.250
During the London Revolution.

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:51.670
That's...

00:15:51.670 --> 00:15:56.500
Don't worry. I was only seven, but I didn't go hungry.

00:15:57.210 --> 00:15:59.290
Because the Intelligence Agency took me in.

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:03.880
Ange...

00:16:10.170 --> 00:16:10.790
No.

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:12.750
Never mind.

00:16:13.880 --> 00:16:14.920
Oh.

00:16:15.330 --> 00:16:16.750
Don't let it bother you.

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:18.960
It was back on the Black Lizard Planet.

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:20.670
Of course.

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:22.920
Eric.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:27.130
We'll be taking you over the Wall next Thursday.

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:28.330
Good night.

00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:07.420
The man being kept at Mayfaire
has revealed his true colors.

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:11.130
Switch to Plan B.

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:13.380
Wait, Ange!

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:16.080
Where are we going at this hour?

00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:27.170
There's been a change of plans.

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:28.380
We're leaving now.

00:17:28.670 --> 00:17:30.540
We can't! It's too sudden!

00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:31.960
What about Amy?

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:34.460
There's nothing to worry about.

00:17:34.710 --> 00:17:36.040
Hurry and get in.

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:56.710
Team 2 to HQ.

00:17:56.960 --> 00:17:59.170
No changes yet.

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:01.250
Understood. Carry on.

00:18:01.710 --> 00:18:03.130
Do you think we'll spot them?

00:18:03.750 --> 00:18:08.000
I've told Eric to refuse to defect
unless his sister goes with him.

00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:11.580
Damn. Those blasted ninja.

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:15.790
Kill the underlings if you want to,
but leave one of them alive.

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:20.330
The Duke of Normandy's orders
are to get their escape route.

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:25.210
Did they go to get Amy?

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:26.290
No.

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:27.920
She's not coming.

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:29.750
You tricked me?

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:31.750
That makes two of us.

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:38.080
The one you really went to for help with
Amy's treatment was the Duke of Normandy.

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:42.500
Your defection was all an act
to lure us out of hiding.

00:18:45.580 --> 00:18:46.830
This is Headquarters.

00:18:48.170 --> 00:18:51.170
The target has vanished!
They're asking for reinforcements.

00:18:51.170 --> 00:18:52.290
What?!

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:53.460
Give me that!

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:54.670
What happened?

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:58.040
Uh, well, we took our eyes
off of them for a second, and...

00:18:58.040 --> 00:18:58.880
You fools!

00:18:59.250 --> 00:19:01.210
Leave someone to keep watch and go find them!

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:06.960
Don't shoot!

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:10.290
You serve Kimble.

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:12.920
I have business with your employer.

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:14.540
I request an audience.

00:19:19.460 --> 00:19:20.920
What the hell is going on here?

00:19:20.920 --> 00:19:24.540
We received a report from A,
and made a change of plans.

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:27.880
We have mounted an attack
against Normandy's ambush.

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:32.130
I guess that's the end of the Duke's hounds.

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:39.580
It always bothered me. Why didn't you say from
the start that you would only defect with your sister?

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:42.330
But then I saw Amy, and it made sense.

00:19:42.330 --> 00:19:44.540
She had the feet of a ballet dancer.

00:19:44.960 --> 00:19:47.670
Feet don't get like that without a lot of practice.

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:51.080
I remembered that when I met you,
you dropped your bag.

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:54.080
and I saw an acceptance letter
from the Royal Ballet fall out.

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:57.210
That's when I connected the dots.

00:19:57.210 --> 00:20:00.500
You weren't going to make your sister defect.

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:10.250
You! Go look outside!

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:18.080
You!

00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:19.670
How did you get in here?

00:20:20.710 --> 00:20:22.670
Public Security Minister Kimble, I presume?

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:26.790
Our boss has some questions for you.

00:20:27.670 --> 00:20:28.960
We're all done here.

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:30.710
Understood.

00:20:31.630 --> 00:20:32.960
Nice work, everyone.

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:37.420
Well, we'd better head back, too.

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:42.670
This is our last stop.

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:49.670
That gun's not loaded.

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:55.670
You're not cut out for spy work.

00:20:58.290 --> 00:21:02.750
Now I can't defect OR go back to my laboratory.

00:21:04.130 --> 00:21:07.460
And your sister will never be cured.

00:21:09.130 --> 00:21:10.580
On the Black Lizard Planet,

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:13.630
we get someone's signature before we kill them.

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:25.670
I'd expect as much from someone
who watched her family's murder.

00:21:26.040 --> 00:21:29.000
That was just another lie to get you off your guard.

00:21:29.750 --> 00:21:33.830
Then was it a lie that your omelets tasted so good?

00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:34.880
A lie, yes.

00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:36.170
I bought them.

00:21:36.670 --> 00:21:39.130
And that the stars were so beautiful?

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:40.630
Probably a lie.

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:46.960
Are you going to kill me?

00:21:48.040 --> 00:21:49.210
No.

00:21:57.960 --> 00:21:58.710
No.

00:21:59.130 --> 00:21:59.750
No.

00:21:59.960 --> 00:22:01.460
No.

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:16.080
It says they found Eric's body in the Thames.

00:22:16.080 --> 00:22:18.130
Why did it take an entire week?

00:22:18.630 --> 00:22:22.580
Because if you die immediately after signing up,
the insurance company won't pay.

00:22:23.630 --> 00:22:26.080
You're very well-informed, Your Highness.

00:22:27.080 --> 00:22:28.710
You're so kind, Ange.

00:22:29.960 --> 00:22:31.040
No.

00:22:31.880 --> 00:22:33.670
I'm not kind.

00:22:37.210 --> 00:22:38.880
Liar.
